   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law, in relation to requiring any entity licensed to conduct pari-mutuel racing and wagering in the state of New York to locate any call centers within the state of New York",
    "basePrintNo": "S4876",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S4876-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1012, RWB L",
    "lawSection": "Racing, Pari-Mutuel Wagering and Breeding Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S4876\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the racing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law, in relation\nto requiring any entity licensed to conduct pari-mutuel racing and\nwagering in the state of New York to locate any call centers within the\nstate of New York\n\nPURPOSE:\nTo require that all call centers which\naccept pari-mutuel\nwagering for entities licensed by the state to reside in the state.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nSection one amends section 1012 of\nthe racing, pari-mutuel wagering and breeding law by adding a new\nsection 4-b which requires that all call centers which accept\npari-mutuel wagering for New York State licensed entities must be\nlocated in New York.\n\nSection two of the bill contains the effective date.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nEntities which are licensed by the state to conduct\npari-mutuel wagering through telephone betting currently handle these\ncalls at call centers located in the state. Any future expansion or\ngrowth in telephone wagering in New York should benefit the\nhardworking citizens of this state.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect\nimmediately; provided that\nthe amendments to section 1012 of the racing, pari-mutuel wagering\nand breeding law made by section one of this act shall expire on the\nsame date as such section expires.\n\n",
